cff-version: 1.2.0
title: net-analysis-lab
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reproducible measurement and analysis of network latency, plus a verifiable
  model of a shared-medium Ethernet. ICMP samples are collected with the OS ping
  binary, passed through a non-destructive quality gate, and summarised with
  Wilson and bootstrap intervals. The CSMA/CD model is checked three ways: two
  independent implementations must agree bit-for-bit, a degenerate configuration
  must match the exact slotted-ALOHA theory, and every slot must reconcile in an
  idle/success/collision audit. Every headline number on the project site is
  regenerated from data/ by scripts in this repository.
authors:
